From: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: restore BPI-R4 LAN port names

The MT7988 switch ports no longer carry generic LAN labels in the 6.12
SoC description. Name the three BPI-R4 LAN ports in the board description
to match the network defaults and configurations retained from 24.10.
Otherwise DSA assigns eth3/eth4/eth5 and netifd cannot add the configured
lan1/lan2/lan3 devices to br-lan.

Signed-off-by: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4.dtsi
@@ -146,6 +146,18 @@
 	label = "wan";
 };
 
+&gsw_port1 {
+	label = "lan1";
+};
+
+&gsw_port2 {
+	label = "lan2";
+};
+
+&gsw_port3 {
+	label = "lan3";
+};
+
 &gsw_phy0_led0 {
 	status = "okay";
 	color = <LED_COLOR_ID_GREEN>;
